"""
Generates the synthetic noise alert pool for the needle-in-haystack correlation demo.

Each noise fragment is schema-compatible with the real case-pack alerts (see
data/cases/*.json) but is NOT part of any of the 7 real attack sequences.
Every fragment carries ground_truth: "noise" plus a noise_subtype
("generic" | "hard_negative" | "decoy") and a flavor ("classic" | "ai_attack")
so the /cluster endpoint can score correlation accuracy without ever showing
these labels to the model or the UI.

Run: python generate_noise.py   (writes ../data/noise/noise_pool.json)
"""
